60,3,1,talk,Midori,,Candidate A offers a regional service team. That solves the ownership gap.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate D is built for transport and deployed on our servers. It fits our calendar.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Candidate B uses a partner for migration. That is the 2018 risk again.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D has an engineering team present. That helps with the admin gap.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate A is a hosted suite. The invoices suggest bundled prices hold steady.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, D is on-premise. Does it handle the yard devices?","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, yes. It is built for transport operators. It should handle our hardware.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, A is hosted. That means no upgrade windows to skip.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, but who trains the depot supervisors? D has engineers on site.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, D is an outright purchase. The cost is just maintenance.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,A has a fixed configuration process. That might stop the scope creep.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,D is deployed on our servers. We control the cutover timing.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,C is modular. That is the cost trap Benjamin described.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,B relies on external training. The supervisors will drop it again.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,C is separately licensed. The invoices show those costs climb yearly.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I prefer A. The regional team ensures someone is in charge.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I prefer D. It survives our calendar and our yard equipment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I prefer A. It avoids the external migration risk of B.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I prefer D. The on-site engineers can handle the admin transition.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I prefer A. The bundled pricing is stable. D is a one-off cost.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
